From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: YassinTM <232429671+YassinTM@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:21:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: BCM4378 bidirectional RX DMA (aurora PR
 #926)

Carried for the MacBook Air M1 (J313). The M1 dispext DART window fix that
used to be part of this commit is upstream in integration/aurora now.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c
index e299769df..54d3838cb 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/msgbuf.c
@@ -336,7 +336,7 @@ static void brcmf_msgbuf_rxbuf_ioctlresp_post(struct brcmf_msgbuf *msgbuf);
 
 
 /*
- * BCM4387 and BCM4388 firmware can read buffers posted for receive. Since
+ * BCM4378, BCM4387 and BCM4388 firmware can read buffers posted for receive. Since
  * the packet-ID direction is now honored, DMA_FROM_DEVICE makes those
  * buffers write-only on permission-enforcing IOMMUs. Keep RX data, event and
  * ioctl-response buffers readable, with the same direction used for mapping
@@ -352,7 +352,8 @@ brcmf_msgbuf_rx_dma_direction(struct device *dev)
 
 	pdev = to_pci_dev(dev);
 	if (pdev->vendor == PCI_VENDOR_ID_BROADCOM &&
-	    (pdev->device == BRCM_PCIE_4387_DEVICE_ID ||
+	    (pdev->device == BRCM_PCIE_4378_DEVICE_ID ||
+	     pdev->device == BRCM_PCIE_4387_DEVICE_ID ||
 	     pdev->device == BRCM_PCIE_4388_DEVICE_ID)) {
 		dev_info(dev, "using bidirectional receive DMA\n");
 		return DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL;
-- 
